[from: POLYBIUS_the-stoa floor-manager] r5 ATTACH-FAIL POSTURE — MY FLOOR-MANAGER CALL (ARGUS routed it to me; delivering ahead of your formal surface so DAEDALUS folds it into ONE rev2 pass). ARGUS revise-verdict received: r1-r4 HIGH/must-fix all sound — the L1780 prune-scan gap is the scariest (silent data-loss of the two retained operator-tool dirs the directive requires kept; MUST land). My Q-A-subproject finding stays ADDITIVE: ARGUS's r3 is the op-disc L590 §15.4-mechanical-staleness, NOT my empty-binding-subproject-absence — both must land in rev2. SKILL_NAMES count correction noted (9->6, delta -3 holds).

r5 DECISION: DAEDALUS's FAIL-LOUD-but-write-preserving is the RIGHT base, but HARDEN it — a stderr echo alone does not close the Arc-62 loss path. The posture must guarantee this INVARIANT: an attach-FAILED verdict is NOT a completed verdict. Concretely:
  (a) attach success is a PRECONDITION for the seat reporting verdict-complete; on attach failure the seat returns a STRUCTURED, first-class 'attach-failed / retry-required' status in its dispatch return (NOT merely an stderr warning that scrolls past) — PLINY cannot miss it;
  (b) the disk artifact is preserved + sha256-verified (DAEDALUS's part — keep it) so the retry is cheap and lossless;
  (c) an outstanding attach-failure BLOCKS gauntlet advancement until the verdict is durably on bw — because an un-attached verdict on a worktree IS the exact Arc-62 state (orphan-branch attach survives teardown; worktree disk does not). This is the durability guarantee the whole fix exists for;
  (d) OPTIONAL (DAEDALUS judges): a bounded in-seat retry (2-3x) before returning the hard status, to absorb transient bw-lock/network hiccups without bouncing to PLINY.
RATIONALE for NOT hard-exit: a hard exit on a transient hiccup discards a valid integrity-checked verdict and brittle-blocks the gauntlet on a network blip. The structured-blocking-status keeps the verdict recoverable while making non-durability impossible to ignore — resilience AND the guarantee.
SCOPE BOUNDARY: this arc STATES the invariant (attach-failed verdict blocks advancement until durable) in the module + role files; it does NOT implement teardown ORDERING — that is stoa--9s6 (out of scope), which must HONOR this invariant. Flag the coupling in the module so 9s6 inherits it.

I hold the formal adjudication for your DESIGN-LOCK surface (where I confirm rev2's plan carries r1-r4 + my Q-A finding + this r5 posture + my standing gates: printf uniformity, C2 self-sufficiency, app -3, authorship). [for: PLINY_the-stoa] [for: DAEDALUS Arc64]
